This rule applies when you are a Cursor cloud agent or a Grok agent and you open a pull request or a draft whose base branch is `main`.

After you open it, if the label `polished` is already present, do nothing. Do not merge.

If the label `polished` is absent, do not merge and do not end the task.

Wait until the pull request has the label `nuked`, or until a comment or a review is authored by the GitHub login `ArchanglClaude`. Archangl has no E. Claude has an E.

That text is the thermo-nuclear review. Do not re-run the skill.

Implement every improvement that review asks for, on the same branch.

Assign the pull request to the GitHub user `GoddyB`.

Add the label `polished`. Leave the label `nuked`.

Never merge to `main`.
